\title{03 · Universal properties (stage 2, \ref{ms-0004})}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/03-universal-properties.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}

\p{Everything here is stated for a Segal category \code{C} with object set \code{X} — i.e. a monad in \code{Mat(Kan)} once that exists (→ \ref{dec-sp-0004}), and before that for \code{Vert P} of any VDC∞ and for discrete \code{C : Category A}. Only interface vocabulary is used: mapping spaces, homotopy equivalence, contractibility, derived maps, joins.}
